{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>ויגז.</b> And he made fly — and so ״כִּי גָז חִישׁ״ (Psalms 90), and so ״נָגוֹזּוּ וְעָבָר״ (Nahum 1)." "<b>ויטש.</b> And he spread out — as in ״וְהִנֵּה נְטֻשִׁים עַל פְּנֵי כָּל הָאָרֶץ״ (1 Samuel 30), ״וּנְטַשְׁתִּיךָ הַמִּדְבָּרָה״ (Ezekiel 29)." "<b>וכאמתים.</b> Flying at a height where they were opposite a man's heart — so that there would be no trouble in gathering them, neither raising up nor bending down (Sifrei)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:10:31.057629952Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}